{
  "workflow": {
    "description": "Workflow B for the personal instance, proven headless with stubs (issues #448 and #451): a test author from one family writes failing tests from the ticket, one writer from another family implements until they pass, then build, tests, lint and the coverage gate each run through the gate shim. Two critics from other families (Vibe GLM and Claude) then review the change in parallel in one ai-dynamic node, and the finding check keeps only findings with a checkable quote. A round with an actionable finding sends the ticket back to the writer, at most twice, in fixed nodes (repair-1, repair-2, each followed by every gate and a new critics round), so no loop exists. After the second failed repair an Opus escalation node judges the ticket and a manual check pauses the run for the owner. No gate node has a failure edge, so a failing gate ends the run in failure; the CI wait is added by a later ticket.",
    "version": "0.1",
    "id": "workflow-b",
    "entry": "test-author",
    "control": {
      "max_attempts": 1,
      "max_rounds": 1
    },
    "nodes": [
      {
        "type": "worker",
        "id": "test-author",
        "executionSlotId": "slot-test-author",
        "provider": "vibe",
        "model": "mistral-large-4-0",
        "profile": "pf-builtin-dev",
        "goal": "You are the test author, from a different family than the writer. Read the ticket's acceptance criteria in the requirement document and write failing tests for them, one test per criterion, in the repository's own test style. Write tests only: no implementation, no change to any non-test file. Answer with one fenced json block holding ok and nothing else.",
        "output": {
          "kind": "json",
          "artifact": "tests-written",
          "schema": {
            "ok": true
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "worker",
        "id": "writer",
        "executionSlotId": "slot-writer",
        "provider": "vibe-study",
        "model": "deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017",
        "profile": "pf-builtin-dev",
        "goal": "You are the one writer. Implement the ticket until the tests the test author wrote pass: change non-test files only, never edit or delete a test, and add nothing the tests and the requirement do not ask for. Answer with one fenced json block holding ok and nothing else.",
        "output": {
          "kind": "json",
          "artifact": "implementation",
          "schema": {
            "ok": true
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "worker",
        "id": "gate-build",
        "executionSlotId": "slot-gate-build",
        "provider": "gate-build",
        "model": "stub-model",
        "profile": "pf-builtin-dev",
        "goal": "Run the pinned gold-band-gate wrapper for the build and answer with its exit status as one fenced json block and nothing else.",
        "output": {
          "kind": "json",
          "artifact": "gate-build-status",
          "schema": {
            "exit_code": 0
          }
